{"units": [{"id": "plane-note5", "translation": "Τέρμα τῆς ἐμῆς [the end of my]"}, {"id": "plane-note6", "translation": "Τάσδ᾽ [these]"}, {"id": "plane-note7", "translation": "Γέγωνε τὴν λοιπὴν [he has made known the rest]"}, {"id": "plane-note8", "translation": "Πολύδονον [much-wandering]"}, {"id": "plane-note9", "translation": "Τῆς πολυφθόρου [of the much-destroying]"}, {"id": "plane-quote1", "translation": "wanderings?"}, {"id": "plane-quote2", "translation": "wanderings have exercised"}, {"id": "plane-quote3", "translation": "show of wandering"}, {"id": "plane-quote4", "translation": "he hurled wanderings"}, {"id": "plane-quote5", "translation": "wandering"}, {"id": "plane-quote6", "translation": "I will tell the wandering"}, {"id": "plane-quote7", "translation": "of wandering"}, {"id": "plane-word1", "translation": "Where do they lead me, far-wandering?"}, {"id": "plane-word2", "translation": "wanderers"}, {"id": "plane-word3", "translation": "To Hades, much-wandering"}, {"id": "plane-word4", "translation": "the end of my"}, {"id": "plane-word5", "translation": "these"}, {"id": "plane-word6", "translation": "he has made known the rest"}, {"id": "plane-word7", "translation": "much-wandering"}, {"id": "plane-word8", "translation": "of the much-destroying"}, {"id": "planema-orth1", "translation": "wandering, error"}, {"id": "planema-def1", "translation": "the same as πλάνη, error or wandering."}, {"id": "planema-note1", "translation": "Πρὸς αὐτὸ δ᾽ εἰμι τέρμα σῶν [I am at the very end of your]"}, {"id": "planema-quote1", "translation": "of wanderings"}, {"id": "planema-word1", "translation": "wandering"}, {"id": "planema-word2", "translation": "I am at the very end of your"}, {"id": "planostibes-orth1", "translation": "traversed by wandering steps"}, {"id": "planostibes-def1", "translation": "traversed by wandering steps."}, {"id": "planostibes-note1", "translation": "Τὴν [the]"}, {"id": "planostibes-quote1", "translation": "the land traversed by wandering steps"}, {"id": "planostibes-word1", "translation": "the"}, {"id": "plax-orth1", "translation": "plain, flat surface"}, {"id": "plax-def1", "translation": "plain."}, {"id": "plax-note1", "translation": "Κενώσας πᾶσαν ἠπείρου [having emptied all of the mainland]"}, {"id": "plax-note2", "translation": "Νυχίαν [nightly]"}, {"id": "plax-note3", "translation": "Φλεγραίαν [Phlegraean]"}, {"id": "plax-quote1", "translation": "plain"}, {"id": "plax-quote2", "translation": "having ravaged the plain"}, {"id": "plax-quote3", "translation": "plain"}, {"id": "plax-word1", "translation": "having emptied all of the mainland"}, {"id": "plax-word2", "translation": "nightly"}, {"id": "plax-word3", "translation": "Phlegraean"}, {"id": "plasso-orth1", "translation": "to form, mold, fabricate"}, {"id": "plasso-def1", "translation": "I form, mold."}, {"id": "plasso-note1", "translation": "Ὅδ᾽ οὐ [this not]"}, {"id": "plasso-quote1", "translation": "the boast is fabricated"}, {"id": "plasso-word1", "translation": "this not"}, {"id": "plastigx-orth1", "translation": "whip, scourge"}, {"id": "plastigx-def1", "translation": "whip, scourge."}, {"id": "plastigx-note1", "translation": "Χαλκηλάτῳ [with bronze-wrought]"}, {"id": "plastigx-note2", "translation": "in the verses of an old interpolator, who twisted the word, which means the scale of a balance, into an alien sense, which he noted from Aeschylus in Etymol. M. p. 674, 20, πλάστιγξ ή μάστιξ, ἀπὸ τοῦ πλήσσειν παρ᾿ Αἰσχύλῳ [plastinx or mastix, from plessein in Aeschylus], and perhaps Hesychius too, who likewise interprets πλάστιγξ [plastinx] among other things as μάστιξ [whip], which very word Aeschylus, if he had written this, would undoubtedly have used, as he said in three other trimeters (Pr. 682. Sept. 608. Ag. 642) μάστιγι θείᾳ, θεοῦ μάστιγι παγκοίνῳ [with divine whip, with the all-common whip of god] and διπλῇ μάστιγι (῎Αρεως) [with double whip (of Ares)]. Nor otherwise Lycophro, who said ἀγηλάτῳ μάστιγι [with driver's whip] v. 436."}, {"id": "plastigx-quote1", "translation": "body outraged by the whip"}, {"id": "plastigx-word1", "translation": "with bronze-wrought"}, {"id": "plastigx-word2", "translation": "plastinx or mastix, from plessein in Aeschylus"}, {"id": "plastigx-word3", "translation": "plastinx"}, {"id": "plastigx-word4", "translation": "whip"}, {"id": "plastigx-word5", "translation": "with divine whip, with the all-common whip of god"}, {"id": "plastigx-word6", "translation": "with double whip (of Ares)"}, {"id": "plastigx-word7", "translation": "with driver's whip"}, {"id": "plastos-orth1", "translation": "falsely for πλατός, which see"}, {"id": "plastos-def1", "translation": "falsely for πλατός, which see."}, {"id": "plastos-word1", "translation": "approachable"}, {"id": "plate-orth1", "translation": "blade of an oar, oar"}, {"id": "plate-def1", "translation": "the extreme and broader part of an oar, oar."}, {"id": "plate-note1", "translation": "Doric form"}, {"id": "plate-note2", "translation": "Πλάτα μὲν οὖν λινορ-ραφοῦς τε δρόμος ἅλα στέγων [The oar-blade then, and the course of the linen-sewn sail covering the sea]"}, {"id": "plate-note3", "translation": "Κατ᾽ ἴχνος [in the track]"}, {"id": "plate-note4", "translation": "thus Heathius for πλάταν [oar-blade]"}, {"id": "plate-quote1", "translation": "of the spear"}, {"id": "plate-quote2", "translation": "having brought the oars to an unseen shore"}, {"id": "plate-word1", "translation": "The oar-blade then, and the course of the linen-sewn sail covering the sea"}, {"id": "plate-word2", "translation": "in the track"}, {"id": "plate-word3", "translation": "oar-blade"}, {"id": "platos-orth1", "translation": "approachable"}, {"id": "platos-def1", "translation": "to which one can approach."}, {"id": "platos-note1", "translation": "Πλατά: προσπελαστά [Plata: approachable]"}, {"id": "platos-note2", "translation": "which is wrongly and contrary to the sequence written πλαστά [plasta] in Hesychius, and likewise in Aeschylus"}, {"id": "platos-note3", "translation": "ῥέγκουσι δ᾽ οὐ [they snore, but not]"}, {"id": "platos-note4", "translation": "to which πλά-τοῖσι [platoisi] Elmsley restored at Eurip. Med. 149, where he discussed the similar error of scribes corrupting ἄπλατος [aplatos] into ἄπλαστος [aplastos]. On the accent see Arcad. p. 79, 13."}, {"id": "platos-quote1", "translation": "with fabricated bellows"}, {"id": "platos-word1", "translation": "Plata: approachable"}, {"id": "platos-word2", "translation": "plasta"}, {"id": "platos-word3", "translation": "they snore, but not"}, {"id": "platos-word4", "translation": "platoisi"}, {"id": "platos-word5", "translation": "aplatos"}, {"id": "platos-word6", "translation": "aplastos"}, {"id": "platyno-orth1", "translation": "to widen, make broad"}, {"id": "platyno-def1", "translation": "See παχύνω."}, {"id": "platyno-word1", "translation": "to thicken, make fat"}, {"id": "platyrroos-orth1", "translation": "broad-flowing"}, {"id": "platyrroos-def1", "translation": "broad-flowing."}, {"id": "platyrroos-note1", "translation": "Πλατύρρους [broad-flowing]"}, {"id": "platyrroos-quote1", "translation": "Nile"}, {"id": "platyrroos-word1", "translation": "broad-flowing"}, {"id": "platys-orth1", "translation": "broad, wide"}, {"id": "platys-def1", "translation": "broad."}, {"id": "platys-note1", "translation": "Ἕλλας τ᾽ ἀμφὶ πόρον [and Hellas around the strait]"}, {"id": "platys-quote1", "translation": "broad"}, {"id": "platys-word1", "translation": "and Hellas around the strait"}, {"id": "pleiades-orth1", "translation": "Pleiades"}, {"id": "pleiades-def1", "translation": "Pleiades."}, {"id": "pleiades-note1", "translation": "Ἀμφὶ [around]"}, {"id": "pleiades-note2", "translation": "It is the name of a constellation, which the Latins called Vergiliae, the Greeks in the singular Πλειάς [Pleias], or in the plural Πλειάδες [Pleiades], sometimes also Πελειάδες [Peleiades]: see what we said under Πελειάδες [Peleiades]."}, {"id": "pleiades-quote1", "translation": "the setting of the Pleiades"}, {"id": "pleiades-word1", "translation": "around"}, {"id": "pleiades-word2", "translation": "Pleias"}, {"id": "pleiades-word3", "translation": "Pleiades"}, {"id": "pleiades-word4", "translation": "Peleiades"}, {"id": "pleiades-word5", "translation": "Peleiades"}, {"id": "pleisthenes-orth1", "translation": "Pleisthenes, son of Atreus"}, {"id": "pleisthenes-def1", "translation": "Plisthenes, son of Atreus."}, {"id": "pleisthenes-note1", "translation": "Τὸ [the]"}, {"id": "pleisthenes-quote1", "translation": "the race of Pleisthenes"}, {"id": "pleisthenes-word1", "translation": "the"}, {"id": "pleisthenides-orth1", "translation": "descendants of Pleisthenes"}, {"id": "pleisthenides-def1", "translation": "Plisthenidae, descendants of Plisthenes."}, {"id": "pleisthenides-note1", "translation": "Δαίμονι τῷ [to the deity]"}]}